<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Counting Ways to Choose Three Balls of Differing Colors from a Bag</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A bag contains \({@number_balls@}\) balls, \({@red_balls@}\) of which are red, \({@green_balls@}\) are green and \({@blue_balls@}\) are blue. In how many ways can three balls be chosen such that among those three balls, two balls are of the same colour and the third ball is of a different color? </p>
<p>Number of ways \(= \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>We can choose 1 red/2 green, or 1 red/2 blue, or 1 green/2 blue, or 1 green/2 red, or 1 blue/2 red, or 1 blue/2 green.</p>
<p>There are \({}^{{@red_balls@}}C_{1} \times {}^{{@green_balls@}}C_{2} \) ways to choose 1 red ball and 2 green balls.</p>
<p>Similarly for the rest, so we get:</p>
<p> \(\left  (^{{@red_balls@}}C_{1} \times {}^{{@green_balls@}}C_{2}\right ) + \left (^{{@red_balls@}}C_{1} \times {} ^{{@blue_balls@}}C_{2}\right ) +  \left (^{{@blue_balls@}}C_{2} \times {}^{{@green_balls@}}C_{1}\right ) + \left (^{{@red_balls@}}C_{2} \times {} ^{{@green_balls@}}C_{1}\right )+  \left (^{{@red_balls@}}C_{2} \times {} ^{{@blue_balls@}}C_{1}\right )+  \left (^{{@blue_balls@}}C_{1} \times {}^{{@green_balls@}}C_{2}\right ) \)</p>
<p>\(={@first@}+{@second@}+{@third@}+{@fourth@}+{@fifth@}+{@sixth@}={@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
